{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":85126,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"73c7f43b-3634-4655-a4be-2f056a54442d","total_cost_usd":0.81131,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60940,"cache_read_input_tokens":20672,"output_tokens":5844,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60940,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5844,"cache_read_input_tokens":20672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":60940,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":60940},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45359,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.045464,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5844,"cacheReadInputTokens":20672,"cacheCreationInputTokens":60940,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.765846,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"The config as flown never leaves the pad — all three ascents crash at ~5.1 km apex — and beneath that failure the ship's 21.4 kg/m² ballistic coefficient puts aerobraking outside the physics, so the endgame's braking-pass mechanic cannot exist at this dry mass however the heat ladder is tuned.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ascent_never_reaches_the_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"The base ship reaches the floor of the band on a ballistic arc with 29.5% of tank left and a 97-second EVA window; the balancer re-derives ~24% at 105 kg dry with a launch TWR of 3.3.\",\n      \"measured\": \"All three sample ascents report reached=false, why='crashed on ascent', with arc apexes of 5,068 m (bottom), 5,104 m (middle) and 5,116 m (top) against a band floor of 50,000 m — 10% of the altitude needed. arc_eva_window_s and arc_fuel_margin_pct are 0 in every case, and climb_peak_heat logs 0 because the flight never crosses 583 m/s. The 2,196 m/s of ideal delta-v in the balance notes is not what the integrator flies: at 3.5 m² frontal area, 1.5 kg/m³ sea-level density and 175 kg wet mass, drag at the 105 kg ship's ballistic coefficient eats the climb before gravity does.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ballistic_coefficient_below_aerobraking_floor\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"Braking passes are a real choice: a skim dips into the upper atmosphere, sheds speed, and comes back out, and the module comes home on one or two passes.\",\n      \"measured\": \"ballistic_coefficient.staged_kg_m2 = 21.4, unstaged 75, against the sweep's own stated floor of ~50 below which 'the atmosphere stops the ship rather than braking it'. The consequence is visible in the skim table: skim_heat_multiplier_measured saturates at the *first* skim in every band — [1, 0.716, 0.716, 0.716] at bottom, [1, 0.519, ...] middle, [1, 0.382, ...] top — because the second skim has no orbit left to trim. The params assert [1, 0.71, 0.63, 0.60]; the third and fourth entries are unmeasurable at this beta. The Researcher assumed 600 kg staged (beta 122); the audited full-hold-doubling rule forced 105 kg, and that single number is what removed aerobraking.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"module_cannot_come_home_at_any_pass_count\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.6\",\n      \"claim\": \"The capacity ladder 222/224/226 forbids the module's plunge (229.6) and admits it on two skims (216.5), so the finale is an aerobraking flight at every shield tier.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Flown, the module's best skimmed peak heat is 545.3 at the bottom sample, 567 at middle and 561 at the top — 2.4x the maxed 226 capacity — against plunge peaks of 603.4 / 726.6 / 909.9. survives=false in all twelve module cells, plate_survives=false, and cheapest_ablation_pct runs 334.8–383.4% of a 100% plate. The rescaling by m^0.48 in the balance notes underpredicts the flown module by a factor of ~2.5. The module also lands at 18.58 m/s in every cell against soft_landing_ms 5 — the tier-2 canopy at 1,150 m² is priced against a claim the simulator does not reproduce.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unstaged_braking_pass_is_never_survivable\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"Braking passes may be flown staged or unstaged and it is a real choice: unstaged costs 3x heat but keeps the engine for periapsis control between passes.\",\n      \"measured\": \"unstaged_braking reports shallow_pass_peak_heat 417 (bottom) and 401 (middle), survivable=false at both, against the maxed capacity of 226 — a 1.8x overshoot, so the unstaged branch is not a choice but a death. The grid agrees this is structural rather than local: unstaged_pass_survivable is satisfied by 22.8% of 5,184 worlds, and not one of the thirteen top-scoring configs satisfies it (every entry logs unstaged_peak_heat 349–368 against the same class of capacity). The 3x multiplier is the mechanic that cannot be paid for.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"optimal_skims_contradicted_at_top_of_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.optimal_skims is {bottom: 0, middle: 0, top: 1} — one skim pays for itself from the top of the band.\",\n      \"measured\": \"cheapest_pass_count is 1 (i.e. zero skims) in all twelve descent cells including every top-of-band load: empty 19.1%, half hold 24.1%, full hold 29.2%, module 334.8%. The single-pass descent is cheapest everywhere, which confirms GDD §5's 'one pass is the cheapest under every ablation keying measured' and refutes the params' top-of-band entry. Feasibility, not cost, is doing the work: at top-of-band full hold the plunge peaks at 223.6 with survives=false against capacity 222, while one skim gives 156.3 and survives — so must_skim=true there for a reason the cost table cannot see.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"feathering_is_priced_but_also_physically_available\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"The escalating thermal toll is the whole brake: a 25-pass feathering descent costs 847% of plate, i.e. it is not available.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The toll does hold — top-of-band full hold at 25 passes costs 12,705,187% of plate, and 13 passes at the bottom costs 15,407% — so growth 1.75 is doing its job. But pass_counts_reachable shows those counts are physically flyable (up to 25 at top full hold, 13 at bottom empty), and peak heat is flat across them: 94 at one pass versus 108 at twenty-five. The brake is entirely economic, with no thermal signal to the player that the twenty-fifth pass is different from the second — the plate simply is not there. Worth knowing because the ablation curve is the only thing standing between the player and an infinite descent.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fuel_margin_and_soft_landing_are_near_unreachable_in_the_grid\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.4\",\n      \"claim\": \"Reentry tuning is a matter of finding the right constants; Sweep 1 settles survivability and the human only tunes feel.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Across 5,184 worlds, fuel_margin_sane is satisfied by 8.4% and full_hold_lands_soft by 6.5% — the two rarest targets in the space. best_score is 8 of 9 and no configuration in the grid scores 9. Every top config that clears both shares a shape this design does not have: dry_mass_kg 200 with fuel_capacity_kg 300–800 (fuel fractions 1.5–4 against the current 0.67), TWR at liftoff 1.4–2.6 against the current 3.3, and sea-level density 1.2 with scale heights 1,680–4,480 m. These are tuning targets — 435 worlds hit fuel margin — but they are only reachable by moving mass and tankage together, not by nudging either.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"climb_heat_lesson_is_unmeasurable\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.4\",\n      \"claim\": \"The ascent crosses the heat threshold at 583 m/s, spends 41.8 s above it and peaks at 47.5 bar units — the player's first, safe lesson in reading the gauge. The balancer predicts this falls to ~23 units at 105 kg dry.\",\n      \"measured\": \"climb_peak_heat is 0 in all three ascents and climb_survivable is trivially true, because the ship crashes at ~5.1 km without reaching 583 m/s. Neither the GDD's 47.5 nor the balancer's 23 is confirmed or refuted — the measurement does not exist. The grid shows the lesson is easy to buy once the ascent works: hottest_climb_peak_heat runs 89.5–214.1 across top configs, and launch_survives_itself is satisfied by 61.5% of worlds, the third-commonest target.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.dry_mass_kg\",\n      \"current\": 105,\n      \"proposed\": 200,\n      \"reason\": \"Raises staged ballistic coefficient from 21.4 to 40.8 kg/m² and matches the dry mass every top-scoring grid world uses; it costs GDD §2.4's full-hold-doubling rule, which the balancer already filed as a catalog concern and which cannot coexist with aerobraking at these piece masses.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"reentry.reference_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 3.5,\n      \"proposed\": 1.8,\n      \"reason\": \"Beta scales as mass over Cd×A, so halving frontal area lifts the staged figure to 79.4 kg/m² — above the ~50 floor where skims stop deleting the orbit — and cuts the ascent drag that is currently ending the climb at 5 km; it costs the Researcher's 2.1 m-across capsule silhouette, which becomes a 1.5 m one.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 70,\n      \"proposed\": 300,\n      \"reason\": \"Puts fuel fraction at 1.5, the value shared by every grid config that satisfies fuel_margin_sane at dry mass 200, and restores an arc to the band floor with margin; it costs the tank's tier-1 upgrade its current meaning, so the ladder below moves with it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.thrust_n\",\n      \"current\": 5200,\n      \"proposed\": 6300,\n      \"reason\": \"At 500 kg wet this is TWR 1.4, the liftoff value every 8-of-9 grid world flies, instead of the 3.3 that drives the ship into its own drag peak; it costs the punchy off-pad feel and lengthens the gravity-loss portion of the climb.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"reentry.heat_capacity\",\n      \"current\": 222,\n      \"proposed\": 300,\n      \"reason\": \"The 222/224/226 ladder was fitted to a rescaled module peak of 216.5–229.6 that the flight contradicts by 2.4x, so the base tier should be re-anchored to the flown empty-ship and full-hold plunges once mass and area move; it costs the 1.8% tier gap the balancer flagged as a squeeze, which is the intended relief.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"upgrades.6.value\",\n      \"current\": 224,\n      \"proposed\": 340,\n      \"reason\": \"Reopens the shield ladder to a felt 13% capacity step instead of 0.9%, keeping GDD §2.5's rule that no tier reaches the module's plunge peak; it costs nothing except that the ceiling must be re-measured after the mass change rather than carried over.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"upgrades.7.value\",\n      \"current\": 226,\n      \"proposed\": 380,\n      \"reason\": \"Sets the maxed tier so the module's skimmed descent is feasible and its plunge is not, which is the endgame's whole mechanic; it costs a re-flight to confirm, because at current mass the module's best skim is 545 and no legal capacity separates those two states.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"landing.parachute_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 72,\n      \"proposed\": 138,\n      \"reason\": \"Holds the 4.4 m/s full-hold claim at the proposed 200 kg dry plus 104 kg hold (v = sqrt(2·304·9/(1.5·1.8·A)) = 4.40 at 138 m²), so §2.3's stated canopy stays a prediction the flight can contradict rather than a solved-backwards constant; it costs a re-derivation of the parachute upgrade ladder, whose 16x span was set by the module.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"reentry.unstaged_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": 3,\n      \"proposed\": 2,\n      \"reason\": \"The unstaged pass peaks at 401–417 against a 226 ceiling and is never survivable in the flight or in 77% of the grid, so the multiplier that prices the steering-versus-heat choice has to come down for that choice to exist; it costs some of the pressure to stage early, which §2.2 wants.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.optimal_skims.top\",\n      \"current\": 1,\n      \"proposed\": 0,\n      \"reason\": \"Every flown cell reports cheapest_pass_count 1 including top-of-band, so the params' cost claim disagrees with the simulator; correcting it costs the appearance that multi-pass is economically motivated, which GDD §5 already withdrew in favour of feasibility.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": [1, 0.71, 0.63, 0.6],\n      \"proposed\": [1, 0.54, 0.54, 0.54],\n      \"reason\": \"Measured multipliers saturate at the first skim in all three bands (0.716 / 0.519 / 0.382, mean 0.54) rather than declining across four entries, so the table should state the saturation the flight shows; it costs the implied reward for a third and fourth pass, which does not exist.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"The ascent failure is the load-bearing result and everything downstream is provisional against it: the descent and committed-descent tables were flown from spawned states at altitude, not from a flight that got there, so they describe a ship the ascent model says cannot exist. Fix the climb first, then re-fly; do not tune the heat ladder against these numbers.\",\n    \"I did not verify that the crash is drag rather than a guidance or staging artefact in the autopilot. Three apexes within 48 m of each other across three very different target altitudes is the signature of a climb that dies before the guidance law matters, which points at thrust-versus-drag-and-gravity, but a bug in the ascent phase state machine would look identical from this output. Worth one instrumented run before spending the mass budget.\",\n    \"The proposed dry mass, area, tank and thrust values are read off grid worlds whose radius (60–160 km), gravity (3–6 m/s²) and scale height (1,680–4,480 m) differ from the locked planet's 200 km / 9 / 3,100 m. They are the right direction and roughly the right size; they are not a flown solution on this planet, and the ratios (beta above 50, fuel fraction near 1.5, TWR near 1.4) are what should be preserved if the absolute numbers have to move.\",\n    \"The proposed heat capacities (300 / 340 / 380) are placeholders shaped to give the ladder a felt step, not measurements. The flown peaks they must sit between will all change once dry mass and reference area move, so these three numbers are the ones most likely to be wrong and the least costly to re-derive.\",\n    \"Beta is computed from the staged configuration alone. The unstaged figure of 75 already clears the ~50 floor, which is why unstaged passes are flyable but lethal rather than orbit-deleting — a distinction the single staged number hides, and one that matters for the unstaged_heat_multiplier proposal.\",\n    \"The simulator is a point mass with a perfect pilot: no attitude error, no angle-of-attack variation, no debris collisions, and a descent planner that finds the optimal entry depth every time. Real players will fly hotter than every peak here, so any capacity chosen to sit just above a measured peak has no margin for the human the game is for.\",\n    \"Nothing in either sweep measures the EVA leg, the tether, the shop, or the campaign's 12–15 run pacing. The economy findings in the balance notes are unflown, and the 97-second EVA window in GDD §4.5 remains a judgement nobody has made in play — the arc that would produce it never happened here.\",\n    \"The module's 18.58 m/s touchdown is identical across all twelve cells to two decimals, which means it is terminal velocity under the starter canopy and is independent of everything the descent planner did. That is physically right, but it also means the parachute ladder is the only lever on the finale's landing and no amount of reentry tuning touches it.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":82774,"ttft_stream_ms":1838,"time_to_request_ms":373,"type":"result","duration_ms":82849,"uuid":"a934be8a-2443-4a28-97c6-d46c9a73be38"}
